Devel::CheckLib only links its probe program in cross builds.

check_lib() runs the program it links to prove that a library works. In
a cross build Makefile.PL gets the target Config through
ExtUtils::MakeMaker::Config, so the program is a target executable, and
running it on the build machine failed with "cannot execute binary
file". textproc/p5-XML-Parser then reported that expat was missing.
Skip the run when that Config names another system or sets
usecrosscompile. p5-XML-Parser requires the fixed tool and removes the
copy it bundles in inc/, which Makefile.PL would load first.
Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted); upstream status: not submitted.

